mysteries come in all shapes sizes and  locations it is fascinating and every  every project that we do is different  david conlon is an archaeologist with  the department of interior what he has  found in the depths of lake mead is  fascinating this is our first real  serious look at what's going on here  near hemingway harbor kotlin has  uncovered the remains of an aggregate  plant a facility used in the 1930s to  make concrete to build hoover dam this  is underwater video of the site the  submarine right here provides all the  pictures it really is an ingenious  little device you have lights right here  a camera in front and propellers up top  and in the back that allow the submarine  to go forward or backward up or down  this is such an incredible piece of  history kay rhodey is a park service  educator at lake mead she always knew  the concrete plant was down there  somewhere in the water but when she saw  video of an intact railroad even she was  surprised to actually see the rails down  there  all of a sudden it was very real and  everywhere we look there's remains of of  nevada's history throughout the weekend  david conlan will guide the submarine  throughout hemingway harbor to see what  other secrets lake mead might be hiding  brian allen channel 8 eyewitness news
 

